      "description": "MGBE-3 Year CLTA (SSM) 26_27.docx.pdf - Google Drive MGBE-3 Year CLTA (SSM) 26_27.docx.pdf File Download ⌘D Details D Print ⌘P View Show Thumbnail Outline Comments Hide comments Show comments Show all comments Zoom Fit 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 200% Insert Tools Find ⌘F Help Send feedback to Google Report abuse Keyboard shortcuts ⌘/ More Save changes Open with Sign in Page / 3 Download Print Zoom out Zoom in Hide file header Previous Next Edit this file Hide thumbnails Hide navigation pane 1 2 3 Approve Reject View Details Request a review Learn more Signature pending Sign Reject View details Review Not Spam Remove forever Not Spam Loading… {\"id\": \"1avYAPaGXF27v6Ob8ast0ZW9qSWz1Bbe8\", \"title\": \"MGBE-3 Year CLTA (SSM) 26_27.docx.pdf\", \"mimeType\": \"application\\/pdf\"} Page 1 of 3 Algoma University is committed to undoing systemic and institutional discrimination and being publicly transparent and accountable. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are fundamental to our Special Mission. In keeping with the Seven Grandfather teachings that are the core values that inform our decisions as an institution, we are committed to creating a welcoming, inclusive, respectful, and safe environment where everyone belongs. These values, commitments, and practices are highlighted in our institutional strategies, including the Strategic Plan; Academic Plan; Research Plan, and EDI Plan. We live these values through the strength and richness that diversity brings to our workforce and welcome contributors from equity-deserving groups including Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, Persons with Disabilities, 2 Spirit, Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, and Queer persons. Algoma University (www.algomau.ca) is an innovative institution that embraces research, scholarship, and teaching to pursue its Special Mission. The Special Mission is founded upon cross-cultural learning between Indigenous and other communities within a spirit of healing and reconciliation. Algoma University’s five faculties — Business and Economics, Computer Science and Technology, Cross-Cultural Studies, Humanities and Social Sciences, and Science — provide students with rich experiential learning opportunities across all of its campuses in Brampton, Sault Ste. Marie and Timmins. Algoma University works to enhance its research capacity through community-engaged partnerships and ongoing development of graduate programming. We welcome those interested in this exciting time of growth! Job Title: Assistant Professor (International Macroeconomics) Position Status: Three (3) Year Contract Limited Term Appointment, OPSEU Local 685 Department: Department of Finance, Economics, and Decision Sciences Location: Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario Preferred Start Date: September 1, 2026 Page 2 of 3 Qualifications, Expectations & Application Process ● Qualifications ● Candidate must hold a Ph.D. in macroeconomics/international economics/international finance or a related field, as well as a demonstrated commitment to teaching and research. ● ABD will be considered only if the candidate completes their Ph.D. before September 1, 2026. ● Expertise in teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in Macroeconomics and International Business. ● Demonstrated relevant academic background, research portfolio, and a record of teaching excellence. ● Experience with remote/online/hybrid instruction is desirable. ● Expectations ● Teach graduate-level courses, including Economics Analysis and Policy and International Business, and undergraduate courses, including Macroeconomics, Financial Economics, and other related courses. ● Supervise graduate students in their Major Research Projects. ● Engage in curriculum development and contribute to the enhancement of the undergraduate and graduate programs. ● Participate in service to the university, such as student mentorship, research advising, and academic committees. ● Other duties and responsibilities as outlined in the OPSEU Local 685 Full-time faculty collective agreement. ● Application Packages shall contain the following: ● a cover letter ● a current CV ● a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., examples of peer and/or student evaluations) ● a research plan (up to two single-spaced pages) ● sample publications or portfolio ● Indigenization, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (I-EDI) Statement ● Contact information of three referees will be requested from the short-listed candidates Note: Application materials should be submitted as a single combined PDF file, with a file name that identifies the applicant. Salary Scale: Assistant Professor $86,467 - $127,317 Page 3 of 3 Candidates shall address their application to Dr. Brett Goodwin, Interim Vice-President, Academic and Research. All applications must be submitted electronically through this link. Applications received by 4:00 pm EST July 17, 2026 will be assured of consideration, though the posting remains open until the position is filled. The position is subject to budgetary approval. Any questions may be sent to faculty.relations@algomau.ca The position is open to all qualified applicants, although preference will be given to Canadian citizens, permanent residents of Canada and candidates with an open work permit to work in Canada. Algoma University is strongly committed to fostering diversity and inclusivity within our community and is an equal-opportunity employer. The university invites and encourages applications from all qualified individuals who would contribute to the further diversification of our Institution, including equity-deserving groups that are traditionally underrepresented in employment (Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and 2SLGBTQQIPA+ persons). In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005, upon request, accommodation will be provided by Algoma University throughout the recruitment, selection, and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. Algoma University welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request to Natasha Miller at natasha.miller@algomau.ca, for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process. Details Comments General Info Type Dimensions Size Duration Location Modified Created Opened by me Sharing Description Could not preview the file There was a problem loading the details. Loading… Back Transcript Close side sheet Copy Add a comment Page 1 Page 1 of 3"
    }
